              "text": "I've completed my review. Here's the full plan:\n\n---\n\n## OpenClaw Tailscale Deployment Plan\n\n### What the Playbook Does\n\nThe `playbooks/openclaw.yml` builds a custom Docker image that:\n1. **Builds OpenClaw from source** (clones the GitHub repo, installs deps, compiles)\n2. **Adds Tailscale** to the container image\n3. **Runs Tailscale daemon inside the container** with `NET_ADMIN` capabilities\n4. **Authenticates to your tailnet** using an auth key from vault\n5. **Container hostname**: `openclaw-gateway` on the tailnet\n\n### Prerequisites Checklist\n\n| Item | Status | Action |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| `vault_tailscale_auth_key` | **Required** | Generate at https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys |\n| `vault_anthropic_api_key` | Likely exists | Already running, should be in vault |\n| `vault_openclaw_gateway_token` | Likely exists | Already running, should be in vault |\n| `vault_google_oauth_client_id` | Optional | For Google integration |\n| `vault_google_oauth_client_secret` | Optional | For Google integration |\n| `proxy` Docker network | Required | Should already exist for other services |\n\n### Before Running: Verify Vault Has Tailscale Key\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tower-control\nansible-vault view vars/vault.yml --ask-vault-pass | grep tailscale\n```\n\nIf `vault_tailscale_auth_key` is missing, you need to:\n\n1. **Generate a Tailscale auth key:**\n   - Go to https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys\n   - Create new key with: **reusable=true**, **ephemeral=false**, **tags=tag:servers** (if using ACLs)\n\n2. **Add to vault:**\n   ```bash\n   ansible-vault edit vars/vault.yml --ask-vault-pass\n   # Add line: vault_tailscale_auth_key: \"tskey-auth-xxxxxxxxxxxx\"\n   ```\n\n### Deployment Commands\n\n**Step 1: Dry run (recommended)**\n```bash\ncd ~/tower-control\nansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.yml playbooks/openclaw.yml --ask-vault-pass --check\n```\n\n**Step 2: Deploy**\n```bash\nansible-playbook -i inventory/